From 1892964ca7597e57c6daa1cc4a528bdb8633d967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Tristan=20M=C3=B5ts?= <tristan@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:08:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] security(server): authorize host-only websocket actions

Previously any connected client could send host-only actions because the
server never checked who sent them. Confirmed with a websocket probe that a
player could overwrite game state ({action:data}) in their own and in other
rooms, spoof reveal/strike/timer broadcasts, and destroy a room with
{action:quit,host:true}.

- data and change_lang now require the room host password (moved into the
  host-authenticated dispatch path); the catch-all broadcast relay for
  reveal/mistake/timer/final_reveal/duplicate/title-music is host-only too.
- host quit (room teardown) verifies the host password.
- host password comparison is constant-time; host passwords are now 24 bytes
  from crypto/rand (~192 bits) instead of 6 chars from math/rand.
- buzz/registerbuzz/registerspectator verify the connection owns the player id
  (ids are broadcast to everyone), so a client can no longer buzz as, reteam,
  or kick another player.
- load_game refuses file paths outside games/ (was arbitrary file read).

Adds auth_test.go covering each check.
